<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  driving.xml — what the accessibility service is allowed to do.

  History
    2026-08-09  A. Sigdel  Created.

  canRetrieveWindowContent is the one that fails silently. Without it the
  service binds, appears enabled, and answers null from rootInActiveWindow for
  the life of the install, with nothing in the log to point at.

  The event types are declared because a service with none is not listed in
  Settings at all. Nothing consumes them: DrivingService reads the tree when it
  needs it, for the reason its header gives.

  No canPerformGestures, and none is coming. Every action turned out to be a
  node action — click, set text, scroll forward — so no coordinate enters the
  app at all, which is stronger than how-the-agent-drives.md promised.

  flagRequestAccessibilityButton is one of three ways in, and the only one that
  belongs to this service. The bubble (#523) is the second. The third is the
  assist gesture, which this comment used to say had been declined — #527
  overturned that and the manifest now declares ACTION_ASSIST, so the sentence
  is corrected here rather than left to contradict it.

  Half the original reasoning stood and half did not. AssistStructure being
  read-only was a cost when the role was wanted as a way to *read* the screen;
  it is not one when the role is wanted only as an invocation, which is all it
  is used for. Displacing the person's real assistant is still a real cost, and
  the answer to it is that being resolvable puts the app in the picker without
  taking the slot: somebody chooses it, or does not.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeWindowStateChanged|typeWindowContentChanged"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagDefault|flagRequestAccessibilityButton"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="true"
    android:description="@string/driving_description"
    android:notificationTimeout="100" />
